<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Mandela returns three months after his last visit, twelve weeks after his first leuprolide injection. He completed four weeks of bicalutamide. Hot flashes continue three or four times a week and are mild; his energy is a little lower in the afternoons, and he still walks every morning. His weight is up 1.2 kg since starting treatment. He has had no breast tenderness, chest pain, breathlessness, or leg swelling, and his mood and memory are unchanged. Fiducial markers were placed and the planning scans done a week ago, without complications. Radiotherapy starts in ten days. Urinary symptoms are unchanged. The audiology test after his wellness visit showed mild high-frequency hearing loss on the left, and he is thinking about a hearing aid. He takes vitamin D every day. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Androgen deprivation</td><td>Twelve weeks on leuprolide; second injection given today</td></tr><tr><td>Side effects</td><td>Mild hot flashes; slightly lower afternoon energy; weight up 1.2 kg</td></tr><tr><td>Radiotherapy</td><td>Fiducial markers placed and planning done; treatment starts in ten days</td></tr><tr><td>Hearing</td><td>Mild high-frequency loss on the left on audiology</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

