    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Prostate cancer, unfavorable intermediate risk, on androgen deprivation before radiotherapy (C61)</content>. PSA has fallen from 6.4 to 0.9 ng/mL on androgen deprivation, as expected. [S]<list><item>Radiotherapy, 74 Gy in 37 fractions, starts in ten days.</item><item>Report urinary burning, frequency, or bowel urgency during treatment to radiation oncology.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Androgen deprivation therapy (Z79.899)</content>. Testosterone 18 ng/dL, at the castrate target. Mild hot flashes and fatigue; weight up 1.2 kg; blood pressure 134/78 mm Hg. Vitamin D is now 34 ng/mL. [S]<list><item>Second leuprolide 22.5 mg injection given today; this completes the six-month course.</item><item>Continue cholecalciferol 1000 units daily.</item><item>Keep walking and resistance exercise for fatigue, weight, and bone.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>PSA on androgen deprivation</td><td>Every 3 to 6 months</td><td>Completed today</td><td>0.9 ng/mL, down from 6.4</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Testosterone</td><td>Every 3 to 6 months on androgen deprivation (target below 50 ng/dL)</td><td>Completed today</td><td>18 ng/dL, castrate</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>25-hydroxyvitamin D</td><td>Three months after starting a supplement</td><td>Completed today</td><td>34 ng/mL, up from 26</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Hemoglobin A1c or fasting glucose, and lipid panel</td><td>Baseline and yearly on androgen deprivation</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Baseline four months ago; next in eight months</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>Bone density (DXA)</td><td>Every 1 to 2 years on androgen deprivation</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Baseline three months ago</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Blood pressure, weight, and cardiovascular assessment</td><td>Every visit on androgen deprivation</td><td>Completed today</td><td>134/78 mm Hg; weight 81.6 kg, up 1.2 kg since starting; no cardiac symptoms</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Hot flashes and fatigue</td><td>Every visit on androgen deprivation</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Mild hot flashes three or four times a week; mild afternoon fatigue; no treatment wanted</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Distress and depression screen (PHQ-2)</td><td>At intervals</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-2 score 1</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Cognition</td><td>Periodically on androgen deprivation</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Mini-Cog 5 of 5 at the wellness visit five weeks ago; no change reported</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Urinary symptoms</td><td>Before radiotherapy, then every follow-up visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Mild frequency, unchanged from the baseline IPSS of 7</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Bowel function before radiotherapy</td><td>Baseline before radiotherapy, then every visit after it</td><td>Deferred</td><td>Not asked today, a deviation from the protocol; the visit was taken up by the androgen deprivation results and the radiotherapy plan. To be checked at the next visit</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Second leuprolide injection</td><td>Every twelve weeks for two doses</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Given today in this clinic</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Physical activity and calcium intake</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Walking every morning; resistance exercise twice a week; calcium from food</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>Reach an informed, shared decision on treatment after hearing every reasonable option, including observation. Outcome by 2026-04-14: Radiotherapy with six months of androgen deprivation chosen at the radiation oncology consultation [